 ],
 "literal": "Listen, may you live long, friend! To mother, / even the high world is small indeed. From his mountain, / with the fragrance-emitting stream that poured in the evening, / the entire root of the glory lily that came in the morning, / embracing it so that its soft leaves withered, / and bringing it to the house and planting it, she did not forbid.",
 "translation": "Listen, my friend, may you live long! To mother, even the high world of the gods is too small to contain her joy. For, when the stream from his mountain, fragrant from the evening rains, washed down the entire root of a glory lily in the morning, she did not forbid me from embracing it until its soft leaves withered, nor did she prevent me from bringing it home and planting it.",
 "modern": "தோழியே, கேள்! நீ டூழி வாழ்க! அன்னைக்குத் தேவர்களின் உயர்ந்த உலகமும் மிகச் சிறியதாகும். அவனுடைய மலையிலிருந்து மாலை நேரத்தில் பெய்த மழையினால் நறுமணம் வீசி வந்த நீரோட்டத்துடன், காலையில் அடித்து வரப்பட்ட காந்தள் செடியின் முழு வேரையும், அதன் மென்மையான இலைகள் குலையும்படி நான் தழுவிக் கொண்டதையும், அதை வீட்டிற்கு எடுத்து வந்து நட்டதையும் அன்னை தடுக்கவில்லை.",
 "explanation": "The heroine is speaking to her friend about her mother's reaction to her actions. A glory lily root was washed down from the hero's mountain by the evening rains and arrived with the morning stream. The heroine embraced the plant lovingly, as it came from her lover's mountain, and then brought it home to plant in their garden. Her mother, observing this, did not forbid her, which the heroine interprets as a silent acceptance of her love and a sign that their marriage will soon be approved. This Kuriñci landscape poem uses the glory lily from the hero's mountain as a symbol of the hero himself, and the mother's acceptance of the plant symbolizes her acceptance of the alliance.",
